#
# Counter-example for math:DistributionParameterizationShape (Rule P6b): a PARAMETRIC
# math:Distribution — one that SUPPLIES a math:hasDistributionParameter — that names NO
# math:distributionParameterization, so the SHACL-SPARQL "supplied parameter with no
# named parameterization" constraint fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:MissingDistributionParameterization).
# Single violation: it names its math:distributionFamily so math:DistributionFamilyShape
# (P6a) stays SATISFIED, and it names no math:distributionParameterization so
# math:ParameterRoleCardinalityConstraint (P7) has no required role to count and stays
# SILENT — EXACTLY ONE finding. (P6a's MinCount and P6b's SPARQL are DISTINCT components;
# this isolates the parameterization SPARQL gate.)
# Back-reference: math:Distribution / math:MissingDistributionParameterization (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecDistributionMissingParameterizationBad).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:parametricDistribution a math:Distribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:normalFamily ;
    math:hasDistributionParameter ex:meanParam .

ex:normalFamily a math:DistributionFamily .

ex:meanParam a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:meanRole .

ex:meanRole a math:DistributionParameterRole .
